From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:01:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 149/155] GreatDANE: document the 404 AUS prompt and the
 /releases/ redirect (round 5b)

5A-M2: the firefox.js comment no longer says dane.surf returns a
"no update" answer. /update/ and /update/update.xml are 404, nothing
is published, and this unofficial build does not serve an empty
<updates/>. After app.update.backgroundMaxErrors (10) failed
background checks, unofficial builds show the manual-update prompt
pointing at https://dane.surf/download/. No server change is made.

5A-I1: https://dane.surf/releases/ 301s to /download/; stop calling it
404. Also note that app.update.url is dead (Bug 1568994) and
application.ini is authoritative, and that no DisableAppUpdate policy
is set in this tree.
---
 browser/app/profile/firefox.js | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 greatdane/README.md            | 12 +++++++++---
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/browser/app/profile/firefox.js b/browser/app/profile/firefox.js
index 487de0b..109e4d7 100644
--- a/browser/app/profile/firefox.js
+++ b/browser/app/profile/firefox.js
@@ -3710,11 +3710,18 @@ pref("browser.startup.homepage", "about:home");
 pref("browser.newtabpage.enabled", true);
 pref("browser.newtabpage.activity-stream.enabled", true);
 // Updates: Dane's own self-hosted, MAR-signed ESR channel (UPDATE-PLAN.md,
-// Option A). Static update.xml; nginx/R2 rewrites unknown paths to a
-// "no update" answer. Mozilla's AUS is never contacted. MAR signatures are
-// verified against Dane's own certs embedded at build time
-// (../updates/embed-mar-cert.sh); the distribution policy keeps
-// DisableAppUpdate until that step and --enable-update-channel=esr land.
+// Option A). Mozilla's AUS is never contacted. dane.surf /update/ and
+// /update/update.xml return 404 (nothing is published; this unofficial
+// build does not serve an empty <updates/> document). Each failed
+// background check counts toward app.update.backgroundMaxErrors (10).
+// After that, unofficial builds show the manual-update prompt (badge and
+// doorhanger) pointing at app.update.url.manual (https://dane.surf/download/).
+// At the 24-hour branding interval that is about 10 days. No
+// DisableAppUpdate policy is set in this tree, so the checks do run.
+// The app.update.url pref below is dead (Bug 1568994); the compiled-in
+// application.ini URL (MOZ_APPUPDATE_HOST) is what UpdateService uses.
+// MAR signatures are verified against Dane's own certs embedded at build
+// time (../updates/embed-mar-cert.sh).
 pref("app.update.auto", true);
 pref("app.update.url", "https://dane.surf/update/3/%PRODUCT%/%VERSION%/%BUILD_ID%/%BUILD_TARGET%/%LOCALE%/%CHANNEL%/update.xml");
 pref("browser.fixup.domainsuffixwhitelist.pepe", true);
diff --git a/greatdane/README.md b/greatdane/README.md
index 8c97242..86154d7 100644
--- a/greatdane/README.md
+++ b/greatdane/README.md
@@ -31,9 +31,15 @@ Decision: per the coordinator's record of its Oct 27 2026 conversation with nowo
   named GreatDANE.app), delete GreatDANE.app from Applications first, then drag Dane in. The profile isn't affected.
   The greatdane.doge start page has this note. Later updates are expected to install in-app once Dane's own update
   signing (MAR key and update server) is in place; until then, updates are manual downloads.
-  The compiled-in and pref AUS URL is https://dane.surf/update/3/... and the details link is
-  https://dane.surf/releases/. Those paths are not on the site yet (404 as of 2026-11-10);
-  this change only retargets the URLs and does not publish update.xml or a releases page.
+  The compiled-in AUS URL is https://dane.surf/update/3/... (`app.update.url` in firefox.js
+  is dead, Bug 1568994; application.ini / MOZ_APPUPDATE_HOST is authoritative).
+  https://dane.surf/update/ and /update/update.xml are 404 as of 2026-11-10; nothing
+  is published, and this unofficial build does not serve an empty <updates/>.
+  After app.update.backgroundMaxErrors (10) failed background checks (~10 days at
+  the 24-hour interval), unofficial builds show a manual-update prompt that points
+  at https://dane.surf/download/. The details link is https://dane.surf/releases/,
+  which 301s to /download/ (as of 2026-11-10). This change only retargets the URLs
+  and does not publish update.xml or a releases page.
 - **Optional cleanup**, only needed if the old app was ever run from its dmg and its privileged installer was allowed
   (upstream dmgInstallHelper.md, old name):
 
